// Nested loop -> O(n) * O(n) = O(n^2)
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
        grid[i][j] = i + j;       // n*n steps

// Halving the range each step -> O(log n)
for (int k = n; k > 1; k /= 2) doWork();  // log2(n) steps
```
Constants like the `2` in `2n` are dropped because growth rate, not exact count, is what Big-O captures.

